<title>POLAND: GM'S OPEL RECRUITS STAFF FOR POLISH PLANT.</title>
<headline>GM'S OPEL RECRUITS STAFF FOR POLISH PLANT.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Adam Opel AG, General Motors's German subsidiary, started recruiting workers on Wednesday for its Polish car assembly plant, PAP news agency reported.</p>
<p>The employment office in the southern province of Katowice, where the factory is to be located, expects to distribute some 40,000 application forms to select 2,000 workers for the plant, PAP quoted the office's director Janina Zalawa as saying.</p>
<p>Opel's official earlier said about 300 people would be hired this year and the rest by 1998, when the 470 million mark factory in the city of Gliwice will be opened. Opel plans to assemble 72,000 low-cost family cars annually.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
